  "note": "Swaps every product placeholder on /pages/ingredients for that product's own live hero image.\n\nWHAT THE PLACEHOLDERS WERE, and two of them are worth recording. The nine images were unbranded stock-style bottles and jars. The Glutathione one carried a COMPETITOR'S BRAND - the bottle reads 'QUINER' - live on a Skingenetix page. The Copper Peptide Day Gel-Cream one read 'SKINGENETIX(R)' with a registered mark the brand does not use, the same stray-(R) fault the first production run was corrected for. Both are gone with this swap.\n\nNO NEW UPLOADS, DELIBERATELY. Every hero already lives in Shopify Files (cdn/shop/files/...), so the theme can reference it directly as shopify://shop_images/<filename>. Re-uploading copies would have broken shopify.md rule 7 - Langify keys translations off the image URL, so an original is never renamed or re-uploaded - and would have created nine duplicate files for no gain. It also means these tiles now track the product pages: change a product's featured image and this page follows.\n\nThe filenames are underscored and long, which check_seo_name would flag - but they are EXISTING product media, not new uploads, and renaming them is exactly what rule 7 forbids. The SEO naming rule governs what we upload, not what we reference.\n\nEach product appears twice on this page - once in a nav row of image-link-blocks, once in its own media-with-text section - so nine images fill eighteen slots.",
